{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d7","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0addc-f5a7-7d72-82bc-9d078a927129"},"sequence":70,"recorded_at":1780531400000135,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0addd-1c80-7071-8fc3-c39a2fdd1512"},"task_id":"01a0addd-1c80-7071-8fc3-c39a2fdd1512","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0addd-1c80-7071-8fc3-c39a2fdd1512","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/TASK-260830-z1yxg9_decision-independent-work.md`.\n1|# Decision-independent progress within the complete RPC task\n2|\n3|The complete original TASK-260830-z1yxg9 scope and all acceptance requirements remain mandatory. The inbound identity association decision in the blocked-outcome packet is still pending human input. The prior membership-only interpretation remains WITHDRAWN. This instruction does not approve membership-only admission, a new SSH identity mapping, an arbitrary expected-peer supplier, a verified boolean, or any other substitute for that decision.\n4|\n5|Continue meaningful implementation of the parts whose behavior is already completely specified by pinned AX v0.5.0 (28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c), sections 11.2-11.3 and 17, without depending on the missing responder identity association. Examples to assess against the exact text and existing owners: typed request/response envelopes and correlation, structural hello map/namespace/cardinality validation, bounded framing and partial I/O, defined deadlines, structured error encoding and historical framing. Implement actual reusable production components and their real public entry tests, not parallel test-only implementations. Retain received values as untrusted; structural correctness is never authentication. Do not expose a working responder or advertise authenticated RPC until the unresolved security boundary is actually satisfied. Do not fill that boundary with a stub, mock, implicit trust, a configurable bypass, or a caller assertion.\n6|\n7|Read the current task, ordering-decision precondition, stopped producer packet and withdrawal, accepted peeridentity/sshtransport verdicts, repository AGENTS.md, Curator-managed Go testing skill, pinned normative text and rule-ownership registry. Preserve accepted prerequisites and the managed Story worktree. No other writer owns this Story. Existing full-task goal remains authoritative; this is staged progress toward that full deliverable, not scope reduction. Subsequent negotiation task219okr and hostile-peer conformance2x16gz remain assigned and fully required. Do not assume namespace/cardinality rules authorize operation dispatch before bilateral admission.\n8|\n9|Before coding, identify which concrete production components are independent of the pending decision and record that boundary. Implement all such useful components that can compose with either eventual approved identity association without inventing a new trust model. Validate their specified positive/negative behavior, relevant gate narrowing and instrument controls. Use real production calls and truthful AC accounting. Unimplemented authenticated consumer rows stay unproven; do not count codec tests as end-to-end SSH authentication or mark whole-deliverable checklist items complete.\n10|\n11|If independent work exists, do it before returning to Stop-The-Line. Preserve its reviewable working-tree delta and task-scoped logs/evidence; update documentation with exact implemented and incomplete boundaries. Run relevant tests during iteration and repository-required full tests/coverage for the resulting partial delta. Do not manually commit on the managed Story branch. Do not publish a completed Change Request, invoke ready-for-review handoff, checkpoint, integrate, land, or mark the task done while the full task remains blocked by the unresolved human decision. At that point attach an updated stop packet naming completed components, actual tests and the exact unchanged remaining decision; retain the complete original scope and board blocked status. If no component is independently implementable, explain its specific technical dependency on the missing association rather than simply restating that association is pending.\n12|\n13|No nested spawns, credentials inspection, real peer contact, SSH configuration changes, direct .task-board edits, or upstream issue176/177 implementation. Primary owns the missing decision and continuation routing. All work is towards the full AX goal; partial implementation is neither acceptance nor delivery.","final_result":true}}}
