nvelope.go, hello.go, inventory.go, envelope_test.go, testdata contracts-v3/v4 and hello v2 fixtures, mutations.py, README — plus UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md and the README.md / traceability / task-board.config.json deltas as tracked.patch): copy the untracked packet files into the Story worktree verbatim, verify each sha256 against the manifest, re-apply the README, traceability and config deltas by hand onto the current tree (the ownership registry is now ownership.v0.6.0.json; the config delta adds the rpcwire fuzz gate to the validation commands — include it in the candidate config, never edit the control root), record the restoration (path, expected/observed sha256, applied/adapted/dropped with reason) in TASK-260830-z1yxg9_restoration-rev1.md, then build on it. Deliver as production code: (1) internal/rpcwire completed for RPC 5.0.0 — exact RPC-4 operations, envelope/body shapes, eight namespaces, limits and the 25-key hello map of Section 11.9 with protocol_version 5.0.0 and contracts.rpc [\"5.0.0\"], Structured Error statically 1.3.0, nonce correlation not identity, no added authentication/trust/config/transport hello key; (2) a host-channel package (for example internal/hostchannel) implementing Section 11.10.1 with crypto/tls only (no custom challenge or record protocol): the initiator as TLS client and the remote `ax rpc serve --stdio --host-channel 1.0.0` responder core as TLS server over an ordered binary stdin/stdout stream abstraction (io.Reader/io.Writer pair; no PTY, no listener), MinVersion=MaxVersion=TLS 1.3, InsecureSkipVerify=false, ClientAuth=RequireAndVerifyClientCert, SessionTicketsDisabled=true, nil client session cache, NextProtos exactly [\"ax-host/1\"], RootCAs/ClientCAs built only from the explicitly enrolled non-revoked non-expired roots of the hosttrust Snapshot (never the system pool), activation refused when the encoded CA DN list exceeds the 65,535-byte CertificateRequest bound, ServerName = the expected UUID-derived DNS SAN HOST_UUID.host.ax.invalid of the selected configured destination (never the SSH endpoint), VerifyConnection supplementing (never replacing) standard chain/name/time/EKU verification with the exact enrolled leaf/root/key/UUID/role/current-trust-state checks from hosttrust, 10-second handshake deadline and 1 MiB incoming handshake byte cap per side enforced even when the peer sends nothing, no application bytes interpreted before local handshake success, hello with its own 10-second deadline and the 8 MiB line / 5 MiB object limits, server finishing verification of the client's Certificate/CertificateVerify/Finished before parsing hello and sending hello success only after current authorization (hosttrust.AuthorizeDispatch with the current committed generation) and identity equality pass (every received hello host ID equals the uniquely verified enrolled UUID; on the client also equals the selected configured destination; local outgoing hello uses the local credential UUID equal to the Config-4 host ID), the initiator validating hello success before any other operation, dispatch and every mutation boundary under the current authorization generation (WithMutationAuthorization), TLS exporters/key logs/secret material never persisted; refusal semantics exactly as written: at most one encrypted Error 1.3.0 failure then close for a non-hello request before hello success or an invalid hello (host_identity_mismatch / peer_not_allowlisted exit 7, incompatible_protocol exit 6 only when incompatibility is actually known), unframeable input and other RPC majors close without a frame, only a TLS alert before TLS completes, initiator-side authentication_failed (7) for known peer certificate/handshake failures, transport_failure (8) for I/O/timeout/unclassified EOF, invalid_config (3) for local config/credential-store loading failure before launch, no new Error enum or exit code; (3) the HC-* gate registry of Section 11.10.4 (HC-TLS, HC-CERT, HC-MAP, HC-HELLO, HC-DISPATCH, HC-MIGRATE, HC-LIFE