{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4c5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0addc-f5a7-7d72-82bc-9d078a927129"},"sequence":189,"recorded_at":1780531400000373,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0addd-8b5c-7901-a574-b7152432d538"},"task_id":"01a0addd-8b5c-7901-a574-b7152432d538","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0addd-8b5c-7901-a574-b7152432d538","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/producer-hostchannel.md 2>/dev/null | tail -c 1500; echo; echo \\\"=== tracked.patch head ===\\\"; head -c 3000 /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/tracked.patch; echo; echo \\\"=== UNRESOLVED ===\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/files/UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read producer tail and preserved docs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"isely in the results (sibling TASK-260830-2x16gz hostile-network tests follows you) rather than an unfinished tree. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 whose tip is the 2ez769 checkpoint (replayed peer/SSH checkpoints beneath it); leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; the preserved packet directories under .temp are read-only inputs — never delete or modify them; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-z1yxg9 and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff. Attach TASK-260830-z1yxg9_results-rev1.md, TASK-260830-z1yxg9_restoration-rev1.md, TASK-260830-z1yxg9_conformance-matrix-rev1.md and TASK-260830-z1yxg9_producer-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-z1yxg9 --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.\\n\\n=== tracked.patch head ===\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex e662afb..1ea37a1 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2352,8 +2352,8 @@ Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\\n [`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\\n the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\\n binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\\n-TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\\n-hello frame and no provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a\\n+TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository has no authenticated RPC hello consumer or provider plugin,\\n+and advertises no Structured Error as a\\n TerminalBackend capability. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\\n [`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\\n an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\\n@@ -2619,3 +2619,29 @@ No durable AX state is mutated; crash/write-idempotency injection is inapplicabl\\n | Transport behavior | `go test ./internal/sshtransport -count=1 -v` | Local process and native config-only fixtures; `.temp/TASK-260830-1tvg8e/` logs |\\n | Transport races and coverage | `go test ./internal/sshtransport -race -count=1 -cover` | Race diagnostics and measured package coverage |\\n | Transport narrowing | `python3 internal/sshtransport/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-1tvg8e/mutations` | Applied compiling overlays, standalone process exits, named failing tests and mutant table; source originals remain untouched |\\n+\\n+## Untrusted RPC wire components (staged)\\n+\\n+`internal/rpcwire` implements typed request/response envelopes, request-ID and\\n+version correlation, structural hello maps and nonce echo, offered limit minima,\\n+`inventory.roots` namespace/cardinality checks, and statically bound historical\\n+errors for the exact pinned RPC 2.0.0, 3.0.0 and 4.0.0 wire shapes. The public\\n+codec returns LF-free bytes for the existing SSH stream boundary; it does not\\n+open a transport or dispatch an operation. Contract profiles describe syntax,\\n+not installed capabilities. Received identities and limits remain untrusted.\\n+\\n+This is uncommitted staged work for TASK-260830-z1yxg9. The full task remains\\n+blocked on the independent inbound SSH identity association decision. There is\\n+no authenticated responder, successful runtime handshake, pending-request/replay\\n+state, negotiated object exchange, or new doctor/capability availability claim.\\n+Other operation bodies remain opaque JSON for their owners to validate. The\\n+existing SSH transport owns partial I/O and configured timeout/cancellation.\\n+See [wire traceability and bounds](internal/rpcwire/README.md) for the exact\\n+implemented surface and incomplete seven-row acceptance accounting.\\n+\\n+| Tool | Exact command | Output |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| RPC codec tests | `go test ./internal/rpcwire -count=1 -v` | stdout; logs under `.temp/TASK-2608\\n=== UNRESOLVED ===\\n# Unresolved implementation decisions\\n\\n## Inbound RPC identity association\\n\\nOwner: primary coordinator for TASK-260830-z1yxg9, within\\nSTORY-260830-1kiyj6. Status: unresolved; membership-only interpretation withdrawn.\\n\\nPinned AX v0.5.0 section 11.1 requires bilateral protocol host-ID verification\\nfollowing external SSH authentication. The outbound transport independently\\nselects its configured Target. The fixed inbound `ax rpc serve --stdio` command\\nand current configuration do not define how the responder independently selects\\nthe configured expected peer before reading its claimed host ID.\\n\\nRequired decision: approve an external SSH identity/invocation-to-configured-host\\nassociation contract, or explicitly accept membership-only inbound admission\\nwith the bound that an authenticated SSH user can claim any listed host. The\\nsecond choice must be reconciled with the existing cross-listed-host spoofing\\nrequirement; it is not currently approved. The independent association is the\\nrecommended route for retaining that requirement.\\n\\n`internal/rpcwire` now provides untrusted structural components. They do not\\nanswer this question or authorize operation dispatch. Full RPC negotiation,\\nbilateral admission and TASK-260830-2x16gz hostile-peer conformance remain open.\\nThe board's `TASK-260830-z1yxg9_independent-stop-packet.md` records evidence,\\noptions, command exits and the preserved partial delta.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5958,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1490,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
