{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4d9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0addc-f5a7-7d72-82bc-9d078a927129"},"sequence":199,"recorded_at":1780531400000393,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7"},"call_id":"call_01a0addd813373eaabb32c087f7c549d","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-5-1\",\n  \"command\": \"cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/producer-hostchannel.md 2>/dev/null | tail -c 1500; echo; echo \\\"=== tracked.patch head ===\\\"; head -c 3000 /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/tracked.patch; echo; echo \\\"=== UNRESOLVED ===\\\"; cat /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/files/UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Read producer tail and preserved docs\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"isely in the results (sibling TASK-260830-2x16gz hostile-network tests follows you) rather than an unfinished tree. Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 whose tip is the 2ez769 checkpoint (replayed peer/SSH checkpoints beneath it); leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; the preserved packet directories under .temp are read-only inputs — never delete or modify them; if origin/main moves before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-z1yxg9 and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff. Attach TASK-260830-z1yxg9_results-rev1.md, TASK-260830-z1yxg9_restoration-rev1.md, TASK-260830-z1yxg9_conformance-matrix-rev1.md and TASK-260830-z1yxg9_producer-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-z1yxg9 --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.\\n\\n=== tracked.patch head ===\\ndiff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex e662afb..1ea37a1 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2352,8 +2352,8 @@ Section 15.1 at 5/7 and Section 15.3 at 2/3, both bound to\\n [`internal/axerror`](internal/axerror); the three undischarged clauses there are\\n the RPC hello obligation `15.1#5`, the bootstrap-row sentence `15.1#6` that\\n binds the provider plugin rather than the host, and the hello-key and\\n-TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository builds no RPC\\n-hello frame and no provider plugin, and advertises no Structured Error as a\\n+TerminalBackend-capability prohibition `15.3#3` - this repository has no authenticated RPC hello consumer or provider plugin,\\n+and advertises no Structured Error as a\\n TerminalBackend capability. The closed 16-capability admission registry in\\n [`internal/terminalbackend`](internal/terminalbackend) gates which operations\\n an admitted probe may confer; it is never advertised on an RPC hello path and\\n@@ -2619,3 +2619,29 @@ No durable AX state is mutated; crash/write-idempotency injection is inapplicabl\\n | Transport behavior | `go test ./internal/sshtransport -count=1 -v` | Local process and native config-only fixtures; `.temp/TASK-260830-1tvg8e/` logs |\\n | Transport races and coverage | `go test ./internal/sshtransport -race -count=1 -cover` | Race diagnostics and measured package coverage |\\n | Transport narrowing | `python3 internal/sshtransport/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-1tvg8e/mutations` | Applied compiling overlays, standalone process exits, named failing tests and mutant table; source originals remain untouched |\\n+\\n+## Untrusted RPC wire components (staged)\\n+\\n+`internal/rpcwire` implements typed request/response envelopes, request-ID and\\n+version correlation, structural hello maps and nonce echo, offered limit minima,\\n+`inventory.roots` namespace/cardinality checks, and statically bound historical\\n+errors for the exact pinned RPC 2.0.0, 3.0.0 and 4.0.0 wire shapes. The public\\n+codec returns LF-free bytes for the existing SSH stream boundary; it does not\\n+open a transport or dispatch an operation. Contract profiles describe syntax,\\n+not installed capabilities. Received identities and limits remain untrusted.\\n+\\n+This is uncommitted staged work for TASK-260830-z1yxg9. The full task remains\\n+blocked on the independent inbound SSH identity association decision. There is\\n+no authenticated responder, successful runtime handshake, pending-request/replay\\n+state, negotiated object exchange, or new doctor/capability availability claim.\\n+Other operation bodies remain opaque JSON for their owners to validate. The\\n+existing SSH transport owns partial I/O and configured timeout/cancellation.\\n+See [wire traceability and bounds](internal/rpcwire/README.md) for the exact\\n+implemented surface and incomplete seven-row acceptance accounting.\\n+\\n+| Tool | Exact command | Output |\\n+| --- | --- | --- |\\n+| RPC codec tests | `go test ./internal/rpcwire -count=1 -v` | stdout; logs under `.temp/TASK-2608\\n=== UNRESOLVED ===\\n# Unresolved implementation decisions\\n\\n## Inbound RPC identity association\\n\\nOwner: primary coordinator for TASK-260830-z1yxg9, within\\nSTORY-260830-1kiyj6. Status: unresolved; membership-only interpretation withdrawn.\\n\\nPinned AX v0.5.0 section 11.1 requires bilateral protocol host-ID verification\\nfollowing external SSH authentication. The outbound transport independently\\nselects its configured Target. The fixed inbound `ax rpc serve --stdio` command\\nand current configuration do not define how the responder independently selects\\nthe configured expected peer before reading its claimed host ID.\\n\\nRequired decision: approve an external SSH identity/invocation-to-configured-host\\nassociation contract, or explicitly accept membership-only inbound admission\\nwith the bound that an authenticated SSH user can claim any listed host. The\\nsecond choice must be reconciled with the existing cross-listed-host spoofing\\nrequirement; it is not currently approved. The independent association is the\\nrecommended route for retaining that requirement.\\n\\n`internal/rpcwire` now provides untrusted structural components. They do not\\nanswer this question or authorize operation dispatch. Full RPC negotiation,\\nbilateral admission and TASK-260830-2x16gz hostile-peer conformance remain open.\\nThe board's `TASK-260830-z1yxg9_independent-stop-packet.md` records evidence,\\noptions, command exits and the preserved partial delta.\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5958,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1490,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c4db","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0addc-f5a7-7d72-82bc-9d078a927129"},"sequence":200,"recorded_at":1780531400000395,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7"},"call_id":"call_01a0addd879273a1a68e8115c031e6a1","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/files/internal/rpcwire/README.md`.\n1|# Untrusted Mesh RPC wire components\n2|\n3|Owner: TASK-260830-z1yxg9 in STORY-260830-1kiyj6. Authority: embedded AX\n4|v0.5.0 SPEC.md, commit `28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c`.\n5|This is staged implementation; the complete task remains blocked on the\n6|independent inbound SSH identity-to-configured-host association decision.\n7|\n8|`EncodeRequest` / `DecodeRequest` and `EncodeSuccess` / `EncodeFailure` /\n9|`DecodeResponse` implement the reusable wire surface. `EncodeRejection` can\n10|frame a supported-version bootstrap failure despite an invalid body; it returns\n11|no bytes for an unframeable identity/version/JSON/size. All output is LF-free\n12|for `sshtransport.Session.Send`; input is one line from `Session.Receive`.\n13|The codec does not open SSH or invoke those transport methods itself.\n14|\n15|The package owns no responder, handshake state, authenticated identity,\n16|capability advertisement, operation dispatch, or pending-request queue. Its\n17|success means structural validity only. In particular, `Request.Hello().HostID`\n18|is an untrusted claim, `Response.OK()` means only the envelope's `ok=true`, and\n19|`OfferedLimits` computes minima without making them authenticated or installing\n20|them on a connection. Repeating `DecodeResponse` is possible; this codec does\n21|not claim replay resistance. Received randomness/freshness cannot be proven by\n22|nonce shape validation. `NewNonce` obtains 256 random bits from crypto/rand.\n23|\n24|## Implemented surface and traceability\n25|\n26|| Pinned rule | Production call site | Named test | Bound |\n27|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n28|| 11.2 exact envelopes, UUIDv7 ID echo; 17.1 containing version first | DecodeRequest, DecodeResponse, EncodeRequest, EncodeSuccess | TestPinnedHelloProfiles, TestRequestRefusals, TestResponseRefusals | Correlation of one supplied request; no connection sequencing |\n29|| 1.6 closed objects and common JSON model | DecodeRequest/DecodeResponse through object/exact | TestFrameRefusals, TestRequestRefusals | Shared canonicaljson validates bytes; opaque operation semantics remain with operation owners |\n30|| 11.2 fourteen-key hello map, nonce/echo and limit floors | DecodeRequest, DecodeResponse, Request.Hello, OfferedLimits | TestHelloRefusals, TestLimitsAndUntrustedIsolation | v2 arrays have 1–16 bytewise sorted unique semvers; selecting mutually supported versions remains TASK-260830-219okr |\n31|| 11.8/11.9 exact historical 24/25-key maps | DecodeRequest/DecodeResponse | TestPinnedHelloProfiles, TestHelloRefusals | Exact pinned 2.0.0/3.0.0/4.0.0 syntax; no automatic major or minor negotiation |\n32|| 11.3/11.8/11.9 inventory.roots 6/7/8 namespace vocabulary and bounds | DecodeRequest, DecodeResponse, EncodeSuccess | TestInventoryNamespacesAndCardinality | Explicit subsets remain valid; results must match requested namespaces. No Merkle digest verification, schema membership or object exchange |\n33|| 11.2/15.1/17 static historical errors and bootstrap framing | EncodeFailure, DecodeResponse, EncodeRejection -> axerror.DecodeBound | TestHistoricalFailureBindings, TestBootstrapRejectionFraming | No responder chooses/sends the error or performs the required one-frame close |\n34|| 11.2 8 MiB line bound | DecodeRequest, EncodeRequest, DecodeResponse | TestFrameRefusals, TestWriterAndAccessorBounds | Codec line limit; partial I/O is owned by sshtransport |\n35|\n36|**0 of 7 full RPC AC rows are proven through an authenticated runtime consumer.**\n37|Five rows have new component evidence (correlation, hello maps/nonce, inventory\n38|namespace/cardinality, offered limits, historical errors). Bilateral admission\n39|has no implementation; connection deadlines/recovery have predecessor transport\n40|evidence only. Codec tests do not discharge the complete seven-row deliverable.\n41|Tests are in the uncommitted task delta, awaiting the managed review/checkpoint\n42|flow after the unresolved decision is supplied.\n43|\n44|Other operation bodies are retained as isolated raw JSON objects, without\n45|schema or permission validation. No caller may dispatch from this library's\n46|success. Object limits are advertised structural offers; object decoding,\n47|negotiated transfer enforcement and durable mutation/recovery remain with their\n48|operation owners. There is no durable state change in this package, hence no\n49|new crash/idempotency behavior to attest.\n50|\n51|## Existing owners and unchanged decision\n52|\n53|`sshtransport` already owns the fixed 8 MiB LF framing, bounded partial I/O,\n54|process teardown and earlier-of-caller/configured RPC timeout. Section 6.2\n55|provides the 300-second default and 10–3600-second configuration range; sections\n56|11.2–11.3 do not define an additional numeric hello timeout. This package adds\n57|no competing timer or stream pump. `peeridentity` retains configured identity\n58|selection/comparison; `axerror` retains error validation and static binding.\n59|\n60|The eventual responder still needs an independently authoritative association\n61|between externally authenticated SSH identity/invocation and one configured\n62|host, or an explicit human decision accepting membership-only semantics with\n63|its cross-listed-host impersonation bound. The membership-only interpretation\n64|is withdrawn. No expected-peer injection, verified flag, claim-selected target\n65|or fallback is introduced here. TASK-260830-219okr and TASK-260830-2x16gz retain\n66|their complete subsequent negotiation and hostile-peer obligations.\n67|\n68|## Verification tools\n69|\n70|| Purpose | Command | Output |\n71|| --- | --- | --- |\n72|| Component behavior | `go test ./internal/rpcwire -count=1 -v` | stdout; task logs in `.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/` |\n73|| Races and coverage | `go test ./internal/rpcwire -race -count=1 -cover` | stdout and task log |\n74|| Behavioral narrowing and controls | `python3 internal/rpcwire/mutations.py --output .temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/mutations` | Per-mutant Go overlay, JSON events, real exit, named failures and Markdown table; source remains unchanged |\n75|| Bounded fuzz smoke | `go test ./internal/rpcwire -run '^$' -fuzz '^FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes$' -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1` | stdout and task log |\n76|\n77|The overlay harness accepts `--only NAME,NAME` for bounded reruns. A kill requires\n78|an actual named failing behavioral test. Compile errors, empty test selections\n79|and instrumentation failures are not kills. Survivors must retain explicit\n80|bounds in the task outcome. No source-only check is added by this package.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
