{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c639","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0addc-f5a7-7d72-82bc-9d078a927129"},"sequence":375,"recorded_at":1780531400000745,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7"},"call_id":"call_01a0adddda7f76b686b9241361930866","text":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-9-1\",\n  \"command\": \"sed -n '46,110p' /Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/TASK-260830-z1yxg9/preserved-before-credentials-260910/tracked.patch\",\n  \"description\": \"Read traceability and config deltas\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json b/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\nindex 039a030..88345f8 100644\\n--- a/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n+++ b/internal/traceability/ownership.v0.5.0.json\\n@@ -3821,7 +3821,7 @@\\n         \\\"ssh-stream-failure-recovery\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease owns the pinned contract catalog. sshtransport provides bounded 8 MiB LF framing, duplex stdio and process failure/cancellation handling, but does not decode hello, negotiate contracts, bind nonces or admit operations. No clause of Section 11.2 is enumerated; its 5 keyword obligations remain unevidenced as full RPC behavior.\\\"\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease owns the pinned contract catalog. sshtransport provides bounded 8 MiB LF framing, duplex stdio and process failure/cancellation handling, and retains configured deadlines. TASK-260830-z1yxg9 adds rpcwire.DecodeRequest/DecodeResponse structural hello maps, nonce echo, ID correlation, limits and historical framing; internal/rpcwire/README.md maps component tests to the pin. No authenticated consumer, bilateral admission, negotiated session or dispatch exists. No clause of Section 11.2 is enumerated; its 5 keyword obligations remain unevidenced as full RPC behavior.\\\"\\n     },\\n     {\\n       \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n@@ -3836,7 +3836,7 @@\\n         \\\"catalog-v050-exact\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"unevidenced\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease only returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3; no clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease returns the reviewed typed catalog rows that reference 11.3. rpcwire now validates inventory.roots namespace/cardinality and matches roots to requested namespaces, without Merkle or object-membership verification or operation dispatch. No clause of 11.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about the 27 obligations it carries.\\\"\\n     },\\n     {\\n       \\\"kind\\\": \\\"section_binding\\\",\\n@@ -3923,7 +3923,7 @@\\n         \\\"structured-error-common-data-model\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Two of the seven Section 15.1 clauses stay unimplemented here. Clause 15.1#5 is the RPC hello obligation - an error contract key must never be advertised or negotiated in a hello frame - and New builds a failure object rather than a hello frame; this repository contains no RPC hello builder at all, so BindingFor is a static table with no negotiation path rather than a refusal of one. Clause 15.1#6 is the Provider JSON-over-stdio bootstrap row, whose only RFC 2119 sentence is that the plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2; that obligation binds the provider plugin and this repository builds no provider plugin, only the cataloggen and tracecheck binaries. LocalFromUntrusted implements the host half of the same row, but that half states no RFC 2119 keyword, so it discharges nothing the clause scanner measures and is claimed for clause 15.1#7 instead.\\\",\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Two of the seven Section 15.1 clauses stay unimplemented here. Clause 15.1#5 is the RPC hello obligation - an error contract key must never be advertised or negotiated in a hello frame - and New builds a failure object rather than a hello frame; rpcwire now builds and rejects structural hello/error frames through its public codec, but no authenticated runtime hello consumer invokes it. BindingFor remains static and no complete handshake clause is discharged by codec tests. Clause 15.1#6 is the Provider JSON-over-stdio bootstrap row, whose only RFC 2119 sentence is that the plugin MUST NOT masquerade a different-major object as v2; that obligation binds the provider plugin and this repository builds no provider plugin, only the cataloggen and tracecheck binaries. LocalFromUntrusted implements the host half of the same row, but that half states no RFC 2119 keyword, so it discharges nothing the clause scanner measures and is claimed for clause 15.1#7 instead.\\\",\\n       \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n         {\\n           \\\"id\\\": \\\"15.1#1\\\",\\n@@ -4007,7 +4007,7 @@\\n         \\\"structured-error-exit-status-fan-in\\\"\\n       ],\\n       \\\"coverage\\\": \\\"partial\\\",\\n-      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. No RPC hello frame is built anywhere in this repository, and the closed 16-capability admission registry in internal/terminalbackend is never advertised on an RPC hello path and carries no Structured Error code, so Section 15.3 keeps that clause unimplemented.\\\",\\n+      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Clause 15.3#3 additionally forbids Structured Error from appearing as an RPC hello key or a TerminalBackend capability, and ExitCodeFor resolves a code-to-exit mapping rather than building either advertisement. rpcwire builds structural hello frames and rejects an error map key, but no authenticated runtime hello consumer exists. The closed 16-capability admission registry in internal/terminalbackend is never advertised on an RPC hello path and carries no Structured Error code, so Section 15.3 keeps that clause unimplemented.\\\",\\n       \\\"clauses\\\": [\\n         {\\n           \\\"id\\\": \\\"15.3#1\\\",\\ndiff --git a/internal/traceability/traceability.go b/internal/traceability/traceability.go\\nindex 4ee55d7..e944866 100644\\n--- a/internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n+++ b/internal/traceability/traceability.go\\n@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@ const (\\n \\t// reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 pins the semantic JSON projection. JSON\\n \\t// formatting may change, but ownership claims cannot be self-minted without\\n \\t// an explicit review of this binding.\\n-\\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \\\"cd00dfd9d6378a7f384e69e540300346ad3ffd72371cc0feebcc58cd1fedfa0a\\\"\\n+\\treviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 = \\\"77d3017b035a62f1e33bfb591ca6f70d2b4b1a1fb06a4baf856914f4dff78625\\\"\\n )\\n \\n var ErrTraceability = errors.New(\\\"spec-to-code traceability check failed\\\")\\ndiff --git a/task-board.config.json b/task-board.config.json\\nindex 1a2b314..873ab46 100644\\n--- a/task-board.config.json\\n+++ b/task-board.config.json\\n@@ -198,6 +198,7 @@\\n           \\\"go test ./... -count=1 -v\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./... -race -count=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./... -cover -count=1\\\",\\n+          \\\"go test ./internal/rpcwire -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./internal/scalar -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzScalarProductionEntries$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzCanonicalizeRoundTrip$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n           \\\"go test ./internal/canonicaljson -run=^$ -fuzz=^FuzzObjectIdentityRepresentationInvariant$ -fuzztime=100x -parallel=1\\\",\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 6861,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1716,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"bash","outcome":"success"}}}
