{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000e995","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0addc-f5a7-7d72-82bc-9d078a927129"},"sequence":4901,"recorded_at":1780531400009797,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"05ccea39-0df0-456b-a475-42ee00a3a1b7"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0ae1a-4402-7320-976f-883818acdb5a"},"task_id":"01a0ae1a-4402-7320-976f-883818acdb5a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0ae1a-4402-7320-976f-883818acdb5a","chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: lines 1-6\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-# Flight Logbook\n-\n-> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n-> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n-\n-## 2026-09-17\n+# Flight Logbook\n+\n+> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\n+> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n+\n+### TASK-260830-z1yxg9 — RPC envelope/hello + Host Channel 1.0.0 implemented\n+- DELIVERED: `internal/rpcwire` completed for RPC 5.0.0 (exact RPC-4 shapes, contracts.rpc [5.0.0], Error statically 1.3.0 via a new axerror binding row) and `internal/hostchannel` built: mutual TLS 1.3 (exact ax-host/1, enrolled roots only, no tickets/cache/resumption), VerifyPeer supplement (ALPN presence, no-resume, verified chain, unique exact leaf/root/key match, profile, trust state), authorized hello both roles via hosttrust.AuthorizeDispatch, current-generation dispatch/mutation boundaries, one framed Error 1.3.0 refusal then close, silent close for unframeable input and foreign majors. Preserved pre-credentials packet restored verbatim (sha256-verified); UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS dropped as superseded by the v0.6.0 11.10 binding.\n+- F1: TLS 1.3 clients report handshake success before the server validates their flight, so rogue-cert refusal tests assert on the follow-up read, not the handshake call; the rogue must read (not write) first or the test deadlocks on the rendezvous pipe while the server blocks sending its alert. Production SSH pipes are OS-buffered and immune; the deadlock is a net.Pipe harness artifact.\n+- F2: Go wraps received TLS alerts as `*tls.permanentError` (unexported, implements net.Error with Timeout()=false) unwrapping to `*net.OpError{Op:\"remote error\"}`. The classifier maps Op==\"remote error\" to authentication_failed and every other OpError/timeout/EOF variant to transport_failure; matching on net.Error alone misclassifies alerts as transport.\n+- F3: `fmt.Errorf(\"%w: %v\", sentinel, err)` formats the cause into the message WITHOUT chaining it; all 37 channel wraps now use `%w: %w` so errors.Is/As see both the refusal identity and the hosttrust cause. This one-character class of bug hid the identity-mismatch chain end to end.\n+- F4: Go caps handshake messages at 256 KiB, so the specified 1 MiB handshake byte cap cannot fire through a real TLS stack; it is unit-proven at the exact boundary (mutant-killed) and integration-proven as bounded intake (4 MB hostile preface reads < 64 KiB and fails fast). Unframeable reads now close the stream (found by the oversize-line test hanging on the half-open pipe).\n+- MUTATION EVIDENCE: hostchannel 1 neutral passed + 22 narrowing killed (incl. hello-ID substitution, stale-dispatch/mutation, cap+1, CA-bound+1, tickets, both TLS-min roles) + 1 documented harmless SURVIVED (client session cache without server tickets); token-preserving census-evasion mutant passes the static census and is killed by the runtime census with the full suite running. rpcwire 1 neutral passed + 34 narrowing killed (incl. new v5-exact). Per-probe overlays/logs/tables under /tmp/hcmut and /tmp/rwmut; packaged into the task outcome tar.\n+- VALIDATION: hostchannel + rpcwire green incl. -race; cover hostchannel 81.6/rpcwire 97.8; fuzz gate added to task-board.config.json and passing; axerror binding row + pinned tests updated; traceability gaps for 11.2/11.3/11.8/11.9/11.10/15.1/15.3 rewritten (coverage levels unchanged, no new clause discharge claimed) with reviewed digest 5102d3bce23e6f27264232332a300dbb89237dc7792673efe9ec039b1219ce08; README figures pin green.\n+- AC: 7 of 7 RPC rows driven through Serve/Dial/Call by named tests (see hostchannel README table). Stated bounds: no ax CLI/SSH launch/provider plugin (computed Config-4 argv only), SSH-carrier parity by construction (no SSH-impl branch), async one-second close via WatchGeneration polling, TLS alert text owned by crypto/tls. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed.\n+\n+## 2026-09-17\n","final_result":true}}}
